    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</em></p><p>A <em>Hag Eye</em> has 3 charges. While wearing or holding this item, you can expend 1 charge to cast @UUID[Compendium.dnd-players-handbook.spells.Item.phbsplDarkvision]{Darkvision} (targeting yourself only) or @UUID[Compendium.dnd-players-handbook.spells.Item.phbsplSeeInvisib]{See Invisibility}. The Hag Eye regains all expended charges daily at dawn.</p><p><em><strong>Coven Sensor.</strong></em> The <em>Hag Eye</em> is usually entrusted to a hag’s minion for safekeeping and transport. As a Magic action, a hag who belongs to the coven that created the <em>Hag Eye</em> can see what the <em>Hag Eye</em> sees if the hag and the <em>Hag Eye</em> are on the same plane of existence. This effect lasts as long as the hag maintains Concentration. Multiple hags in the coven can see through the <em>Hag Eye</em> simultaneously.</p><p><em><strong>Creating a Hag Eye.</strong></em> Only a hag coven can craft this item, which is made from a real eye coated in varnish and often fitted to a pendant or another wearable item. A hag coven can have only one <em>Hag Eye</em> at a time, and creating a new one requires all three members of the coven to perform a special rite. This rite takes 1 hour, and the hags can’t perform it if one or more of them has the &amp;Reference[Incapacitated apply=false] condition. If the hags take any other actions during this rite, the rite fails and ends.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
